It is nullified, etc. And we do not say it has permitted status for roasting, for for roasting it was never forbidden — and compare to Yevamot 2a, unlike Rif chapter 3 regarding bread baked with roasting, and siman 102 seif 4 in hagahah who gave another reason, and Darkei Moshe there. And even though min b'she'eino mino is not nullified, as stated end of siman 109 — this case is different, for it is only a stringency in general. Shach.<br>
And even, etc. As stated above siman 101 seif 2.<br>
And likewise, etc. As follows s.k. 57, that he left in doubt; and Peri Chadash wrote that since blood in cooking is d'rabbanan, even min b'she'eino mino is nullified, for it is like min b'mino d'oraisa (and this is Shach's view in siman 109 s.k. 9, and see our Rabbi there s.k. 8, that we do not hold thus):}
